      {
        "id": 162663,
        "name": "UXM266",
        "username": "UXM266",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/uxm266/{size}/1966_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-15T14:46:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"josmun26\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/5e9695/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> josmun26:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Sorry I'm coming late to the party, but as a previous owner of an earlier version of the Enhanced Edition, I wanted to add a few things that caused me to drop $40 on this third printing.1. The third printing's cards are cut to the correct length.&nbsp; Earlier&nbsp;cards were cut just a bit longer at the top than they should have been.&nbsp; I've heard this has made&nbsp;issues with sleeving when using \"perfect fit\" sleeves&nbsp;(although I don't sleeve so I can't verify this).&nbsp;&nbsp;The difference was&nbsp;also noticable when making&nbsp;the support deck of&nbsp;un-used hero character cards&nbsp;for the two-player variant that included hero cards from expansions.&nbsp; Also, I ordered replacement cards for the re-printed errata&nbsp;cards (see point 3), and I couldn't use them with my earlier version as the lengths were different.2. The box of the third printing is of the correct width.&nbsp; Earlier&nbsp;boxes were made just a bit more narrow than the expansion boxes, which I&nbsp;heard caused issues with storing&nbsp;sleeved cards (again, I can't verify this)3. The errata cards are included in the third printing.&nbsp; About 4 of the cards, which were re-printed with errata (ex. Fanatic's \"Chastise\"), are included in this version.Just sharing in case anyone else with an earlier version&nbsp;might benefit from this info.Thanks</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The 3rd printing with these changes exist? or this just a \"wish-to-have\"?</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:43:31.584Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
